/**
	Whether the script set the rate of the voice, with set_rate or the rate property, rather than the voice following the platform's own setting.
	bool tts_voice::rate_set;
	## Remarks:
		This property is read-only. Until the rate is set, the voice speaks at the rate it starts with: on Windows and Android the rate chosen in the system's speech settings, which Android follows when the user changes it; on Apple platforms Apple's default rate, as Apple doesn't let apps read the user's speech settings; with the builtin voice its own default. Speech Dispatcher on Linux speaks at the rate of its own configuration, and doesn't take a rate set here.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	alert("Before", "rate_set: " + v.rate_set);
	v.rate = 2;
	alert("After", "rate_set: " + v.rate_set);
}
